  "worked_solution": "To raise the product of two numbers to the power of $3$, we can raise each number to the power of $3,$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n(4\\times 19)^{3}=({4}^{3})\\times ({19}^{3})={4}^{3}\\times {19}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, using, ${4}^{3}=64,$ we can simplify:\n\n$$\n{4}^{3}\\times {19}^{3}=64\\times {19}^{3}\n$$",
